To: Eden Luzon <edenl@nayax.com>,<support@combtas.', 3);
INSERT INTO [dbo].[knowledge_chunks] ([id],[document_id],[content],[chunk_index]) VALUES (NEWID(), 'f616c726-392b-408c-9801-ba3a30dd6f84', N'erin decision.
I think we should keep it mandatory filed. @Enon Halperin FYI
From: Oren Tepper <orent@nayax.com>
Sent: 17:30 Sunday 01 December, 2024
To: Eden Luzon <edenl@nayax.com>,<support@combtas.com>, Enon Halperin <enonh@nayax.com>
Cc: Hila Tamir <hilat@tripex.io>
Subject: Re: TAS Expense without a receipt
Folks,
Where are we with this? Unfortunately FP&A doesn''t run the world there are many circumstances where an
expense doesn''t have a receipt.
This is common practice in any company so it isn''t a question of whether we need to allow it or not. What we should
do is to allow it and give the user the option to explain why.
Of course once we both approve reports we need to see whether this is an exceptional case or something relates to
the nature of the country (e.g. good luck with getting Taxi receipts in many APAC countries like Philippines,
Indonesia etc.).
However the system should definitely allow it, and we have the option do deny such expense.
Oren
Note from:', 4);
